Models downloaded by `astratra-models fetch`
============================================

No model weight is part of this package or redistributed by it. The command
downloads each file from Hugging Face at the commit pinned in
models-manifest.json, under the licence of the model's publisher. Each licence
below allows commercial use.

embed       Xenova/bge-m3 (ONNX conversion of BAAI/bge-m3)                  MIT
rerank      onnx-community/gte-multilingual-reranker-base (ONNX conversion
            of Alibaba-NLP/gte-multilingual-reranker-base, Apache-2.0)      Apache-2.0
nli         MoritzLaurer/mDeBERTa-v3-base-xnli-multilingual-nli-2mil7        MIT
entities    urchade/gliner_multi-v2.1                                        Apache-2.0
            microsoft/mdeberta-v3-base (configuration and tokenizer only)    MIT
transcribe  Systran/faster-whisper-small (conversion of openai/whisper-small) MIT
transcribe_base (optional, fetched by name only)
            Systran/faster-whisper-base (conversion of openai/whisper-base)  MIT
injection   Horizon-Labs/prompt-injection-guard-small                        Apache-2.0
moderation  Horizon-Labs/content-safety-guard-small                          Apache-2.0

Credits for the guard models
----------------------------
Both are fine-tuned from jhu-clsp/mmBERT-small (MIT). Their publisher states
that they were trained on permissively licensed data only. Among the sources
named on the model cards, these ask for attribution:
  - NVIDIA Nemotron-Safety-Guard-Dataset-v3 (CC-BY-4.0), used by the
    content-safety model; NVIDIA NeMo/Nemotron agentic and jailbreak sets
    (CC-BY-4.0), used by the prompt-injection model;
  - WildChat-1M (ODC-BY), FineWeb-Edu and FineWeb-2 (ODC-BY);
  - Civil Comments (CC0), OpenAssistant oasst2 and Aya (Apache-2.0).
Training data and the model cards are at the Hugging Face addresses above.

Notice for the prompt-injection model: it flags text that tries to change what
an AI does; it is one signal, not a guarantee. The content-safety model is weak
on the `sexual_minors` category: never use it alone for child-safety or legal
compliance.
